\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end prediction pipeline. ACLED conflict events from Nigeria, Mexico, and Myanmar (2018--2024) are aggregated to region-month units and transformed into event-based features (solid border) and actor network features (dashed border; 12 metrics providing no incremental predictive value beyond the event-based features). Six-month sliding windows produce temporal sequences for LSTM processing. The strict temporal split prevents information leakage, with training on 2018--2022 and testing on 2023--2024. Nine ablation configurations systematically test feature contributions across 27 experiments. The recommended model (Events Only, highlighted) uses 4 features to achieve AUPRC 0.745.}}{9}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{9}{End-to-end prediction pipeline. ACLED conflict events from Nigeria, Mexico, and Myanmar (2018--2024) are aggregated to region-month units and transformed into event-based features (solid border) and actor network features (dashed border; 12 metrics providing no incremental predictive value beyond the event-based features). Six-month sliding windows produce temporal sequences for LSTM processing. The strict temporal split prevents information leakage, with training on 2018--2022 and testing on 2023--2024. Nine ablation configurations systematically test feature contributions across 27 experiments. The recommended model (Events Only, highlighted) uses 4 features to achieve AUPRC 0.745}{figure.1}{}}
