\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Feature ablation study results sorted by test AUPRC (mean $\pm $ SD across 3 random seeds). The Events Only model ($\star $, 4 features) matches or outperforms all network-augmented configurations, including the Full Model with 16 features. Adding any network feature category provides no meaningful improvement (all $\Delta \leq \pm 0.004$). The dashed vertical line marks the Full Model baseline. Removing past disappearances causes the largest single-feature drop ($-$10.1\%), but the model retains substantial predictive power (0.666) well above random (0.483), providing evidence of forecasting value when the lagged disappearance feature is withheld.}}{19}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ablations}{{3}{19}{Feature ablation study results sorted by test AUPRC (mean $\pm $ SD across 3 random seeds). The Events Only model ($\star $, 4 features) matches or outperforms all network-augmented configurations, including the Full Model with 16 features. Adding any network feature category provides no meaningful improvement (all $\Delta \leq \pm 0.004$). The dashed vertical line marks the Full Model baseline. Removing past disappearances causes the largest single-feature drop ($-$10.1\%), but the model retains substantial predictive power (0.666) well above random (0.483), providing evidence of forecasting value when the lagged disappearance feature is withheld}{figure.3}{}}
